{#
The provider chooser shared by both admin credential steps.

Buttons, not links, and that is the whole point: switching used to be a plain
navigation, which threw away whatever had been typed for the provider you were
leaving. Filling in the Google client id and then clicking Microsoft lost it
silently. Now the switch submits the step first, so what you entered is saved
and you come back to it.

Every field on these forms is optional, so a half-filled provider saves as a
half-filled provider rather than refusing. type="button" keeps Next as the
form's default submit — otherwise Enter in a text field would switch provider.

The list is every provider, always. It used to be only the ones still needing
attention, which combined badly with save-on-switch: the provider you had just
left acquired a row, stopped counting as outstanding, and disappeared from the
list you were looking at. A tick marks the ones that are set up.

Wraps onto as many rows as it needs, and does NOT scroll sideways. There are
eight integration providers now, which is past what fits across a dialog even
on a desktop, and the row used to overflow: the wizard's body is
`overflow-y-auto`, and CSS computes the other axis to `auto` as soon as one is
not `visible`, so the whole modal grew a horizontal scrollbar and the step's
form slid out from under the buttons. The progress rail above still scrolls
instead of wrapping, and that is not an inconsistency — it is one line of
numbered pills whose reflow would move the body mid-wizard, whereas these are a
tab list that is meant to be read as a block.

`whitespace-nowrap` on the button, not a non-breaking space in the label: the
names come from Integration\Provider::label() and Account\MailProvider::label(),
which are brand names deliberately left untranslated, so there is no catalogue
entry to put a U+00A0 into and "Google Drive" would have to be spelled with an
invisible character in PHP. The rule is also the one actually wanted — no
provider name breaks mid-name, whatever it is called — rather than a fix
applied one name at a time.
#}
<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 mb-5"
     role="tablist"
     data-controller="onboarding--form-nav">

    <input type="hidden" name="switch_to" value="" data-onboarding--form-nav-target="field">

    {% for option in providers %}
        <button
            type="button"
            id="onboarding-provider-{{ option.value }}"
            role="tab"
            aria-selected="{{ option.value == provider.value ? 'true' : 'false' }}"
            data-value="{{ option.value }}"
            data-action="click->onboarding--form-nav#go"
            class="inline-flex shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap items-center gap-2 h-8 px-3 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium border transition-colors cursor-pointer
                   {% if option.value == provider.value %}
                     border-accent bg-accent/10 text-accent
                   {% else %}
                     border-field bg-field text-ink-soft hover:bg-hover
                   {% endif %}"
        >
            <i class="{{ option.icon }} text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            {{ option.label }}
            {% if decided[option.value]|default(false) %}
                <i class="fa-solid fa-check text-[10px] text-success" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            {% endif %}
        </button>
    {% endfor %}
</div>
